<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Eid Download - third-party licenses</title>
<style>body{font-family:sans-serif;max-width:60em;margin:2em auto;padding:0 1em}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;background:#f4f4f4;padding:1em}</style></head>
<body>
<h1>Third-party licenses</h1>
<p>Eid Download is MIT licensed (see LICENSE.txt). It includes the following Rust crates, each under
its own license. The source code of every crate listed here, including those under MPL-2.0, is
available unmodified from crates.io at the linked address.</p>
<h2>Overview</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}<li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}</ul>
{{#each licenses}}
<h2 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h2>
<p>Used by:</p>
<ul>
{{#each used_by}}<li><a href="https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}/{{crate.version}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
{{/each}}</ul>
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
{{/each}}
</body>
</html>
